{"ts": "2026-09-19T05:24:57Z", "issue": 3, "run_id": "20260919-0229-to3m", "kind": "cross_domain_probe", "model": "pythia-70m-deduped", "revision": null, "dtype": "float32", "sae": "pythia-70m-deduped-res-sm", "layer": 3, "feature_id": null, "hook": "blocks.3.hook_resid_post", "inputs_a": {"domain": "cooking", "source": "Corpus/cross_domain.json, generated by gen_cross_domain.py", "n": 120, "median_tokens": 18, "example": "A smooth steam , knife braise , the rich broth boil , meal blend , rosemary ladle"}, "inputs_b": {"domain": "astronomy", "source": "Corpus/cross_domain.json, generated by gen_cross_domain.py", "n": 120, "median_tokens": 19, "example": "redshift : elliptical quasar ; remnant propagate -> spiral luminosity ; corona orbit ( telescope )"}, "activation_a": null, "activation_b": null, "input_disjointness": {"shared_tokenizer_ids": 0, "method": "tokenizer id intersection, add_special_tokens=False", "note": "each domain also has its own glue tokens, so no surface token is shared between the two sets"}, "null_model": "pairing permutation, N_PERM=400: a feature's matched-pairing co-activation rate is standardized against its own mean/sd over shuffled pairings", "correction": "family-wise max-statistic on the standardized statistic: 95th percentile over permutations of the max per-feature z (DEC-016 family). BH-FDR not used.", "n": 793, "statistic": "standardized per-feature cross-domain co-activation z; family-wise cutoff z=4.41", "result": {"n_family": 793, "best_z": 3.1, "best_feature": 1478, "cutoff_z": 4.41, "n_survivors": 0, "raw_best_rate": 0.3667, "raw_cutoff": 0.3917, "per_feature_threshold_variant": {"n_family": 66, "best_z": 3.37, "cutoff_z": 4.97, "n_survivors": 0}, "positive_control": {"planted_token": "Zorblat", "planted_rate": 0.1, "n_pairs": 12, "recovered": true, "best_z": 11.3, "cutoff_z": 4.47, "injected_feature": 11068, "injected_feature_rate": 0.1}, "clusters_at_cos_0.5": 740, "largest_cluster": 11}, "p_corrected": null, "confounds_checked": ["shared_literal_tokens", "shared_sequence_position", "catch_all_features", "punctuation_glue_features", "feature_splitting_clustering", "injected_positive_control_recovery"], "confounds_fired": [], "paraphrase_controls": ["zero_shared_tokens"], "paraphrase_survived": true, "intervention": null, "causal_claim": false, "verdict": "null", "note": "NULL, and the null is interpretable: the injected positive control recovers, so the detector is not asleep. With 120 token-disjoint cooking vs astronomy passages, no SAE feature at layer 3 co-activates across the two domains more than chance (best z=3.10 vs family-wise cutoff z=4.41; 0 survivors). This is the expected result at this scale and is informative about the method's signal-to-noise, not a disproof of cross-domain structure. TWO STATISTIC FAILURES found by running, both retained: (1) a raw co-activation-rate family-max cutoff could not be cleared by a 10% injected signal (0.3417 vs 0.3750) because high-firing features co-fire at ~0.37 by chance - DEC-016's structural failure in a new place; (2) a per-feature 95th-percentile firing threshold excluded sparse planted signals. Standardizing per feature fixed (1): positive control recovers at z=11.30 vs 4.47. paraphrase_survived=true refers to the zero-shared-token input gate; a genuine paraphrase control is #6, which found weak bridging. Feature absorption caveat applies: a null may reflect SAE representational limits rather than absence of structure (PRIOR_ART 4). Unusual activation is not evidence of correctness."}
